# Sync Documentation Changes

- After modifying repository documentation or learning materials, verify the changes, create a descriptive Git commit, and push the current branch to its configured GitHub remote.
- Include all completed changes that belong to the current task, while preserving unrelated user changes.
- Never commit secrets, local `.env` files, credentials, downloaded model weights, caches, or generated private data.
- Do not force-push or overwrite remote history.
- If commit or push fails, preserve the local work and clearly report the cause and current Git state.
